    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A strange girl, alone in a thick fog, floats in the water after a heavy storm...<br>She doesn't seem to speak my language... and, even though helping someone into a boat is a universal concept, when I offer her my hand, she looks at me as though she doesn't know what to make of me.<br>Her skin and hair feel off to the touch, and she's a strange color...<br>She doesn't seem quite human, and when I bring her into my boat, she bites me... assuming that I'm food.<br>... She seems to have a numbing venom, when she bites me...<br>But when I look into her eyes and she looks into mine, I know she's a person with a soul.<br>There's a tenderness, there... and despite the language barrier, I know part of her sees me and understands me. <br>Showing her a little kindness, she understands that I'm far from food.<br>And, after I lose consciousness... she doesn't eat me.<br>In fact... she stays in the boat and waits for me to wake up, sad about what happened.<br>I expected to be eaten... or else abandoned.<br>But now... I'm alone with a heartfelt girl.<br><br>A Lily from the Lightless Water is a romance visual novel about a young man who finds a loving plant girl, out on the water of a bay. He takes her in, clothes her, and love between them blooms. <br><br>A Lily from the Lightless Water is around 20,000 words long, and is a project developed by a sole developer. Any support is appreciated, and I hope you enjoy this love story.   <br><br>This is a simple story, with no choices - no walkthrough is needed to get the intended ending.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A strange girl, alone in a thick fog, floats in the water after a heavy storm...<br>She doesn't seem to speak my language... and, even though helping someone into a boat is a universal concept, when I offer her my hand, she looks at me as though she doesn't know what to make of me.<br>Her skin and hair feel off to the touch, and she's a strange color...<br>She doesn't seem quite human, and when I bring her into my boat, she bites me... assuming that I'm food.<br>... She seems to have a numbing venom, when she bites me...<br>But when I look into her eyes and she looks into mine, I know she's a person with a soul.<br>There's a tenderness, there... and despite the language barrier, I know part of her sees me and understands me. <br>Showing her a little kindness, she understands that I'm far from food.<br>And, after I lose consciousness... she doesn't eat me.<br>In fact... she stays in the boat and waits for me to wake up, sad about what happened.<br>I expected to be eaten... or else abandoned.<br>But now... I'm alone with a heartfelt girl.<br><br>A Lily from the Lightless Water is a romance visual novel about a young man who finds a loving plant girl, out on the water of a bay. He takes her in, clothes her, and love between them blooms. <br><br>A Lily from the Lightless Water is around 20,000 words long, and is a project developed by a sole developer. Any support is appreciated, and I hope you enjoy this love story.   <br><br>This is a simple story, with no choices - no walkthrough is needed to get the intended ending.</p>",
